fact WorkItem(id: "WI-284", description: some(value: "Typed-occurrence substrate + min_sort. The typer currently DISCARDS each occurrence's inferred type (TypeResult.ty); NodeKind::Expr keeps only classification + resolved_type_args, no type field. Make the typer KEEP each occurrence's type (typed expressions, as any statically-typed compiler's typed AST). Storage is an impl detail (lean: a RefCell field on NodeKind::Expr alongside classification; alternatives: side table keyed by occurrence, or asserted reflect type_of facts). Add min_sort(occ) = sort_functor_of(kept type) — sort_functor_of already exists (unwraps parameterized/sort_ref to the sort head); returns None on an unresolved type var. min_sort is an expression-accepting (compile-time) reader, never a runtime/typeof goal; it is the least declared sort the occurrence inhabits (sort_head of its inferred type). FOUNDATION for all type-directed simp/dot firing (WI-283/WI-279) and also benefits codegen/eval/IR (which re-derive types today). Refs: docs/design/simp-rewrite-design.md 2.2(4)/5.4, docs/design/simp-dot-finding.md, docs/proposals/043-simp-rewrite.md 4.2. Acceptance: each typed occurrence carries its inferred type; min_sort(occ) returns the least declared sort (3 -> Int; cons(1,nil()) -> List; a free-standing entity value -> its sort) and None on an unresolved type var; cargo-test green."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-05-22T16:14:00Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-284", author: "user", content: "Delivered (commit pending). (a) inferred_type: RefCell<Option<TermId>> on NodeKind::Expr — the 3rd typer annotation beside classification (WI-231)/resolved_type_args (WI-272); that precedent settled D2 (field, not side-table: a side-table would be Rc-pointer-keyed and desync on simp rebuilds); + set_inferred_type/inferred_type accessors. (b) Typer KEEPS each occurrence type via a results-neutral TypeBuildFrame::Stamp{occ} pushed UNDER every Visit by a new push_visit helper: it peeks results.last() and writes the type when the node TypeResult finalizes — uniform across iterative (Apply/Constructor/Let/Match/Lambda) and recursive-helper (If/collection-literal, which re-enter type_check_node) arms, exactly once per node; drains and the results.len()==1 assert unperturbed. (c) pub sort_functor_of(kb,ty)->Option<Symbol> (unwraps sort_ref / parameterized base / bare Ref; None on type var) + pub min_sort(kb,occ)=sort_functor_of(occ.inferred_type()). CORRECTION: sort_functor_of/min_sort did NOT pre-exist (WI text stale; reverted with the WI-278 c/e increment) — rebuilt on extract_sort_ref_sym + type_functor_name. Tests (tests/include/wi284_min_sort_test.rs, 5): 3->Int; cons(1,nil())->List + child stamping; entity red->Color; unresolved type var->None; sort_functor_of(type var)->None. Suite: anthill-core 908/0; anthill-core+smt-gen 977/0. code-review (max, 3 angles): Stamp invariant verified across every frame + error path; field addition clean (only 2 constructors build it, Drop unaffected since TermId is Copy, consumers use ..); min_sort correct for all cases. LATENT (not live): sort_functor_of returns None for the SLD-canonical Fn(S,[],[..]) shape + qualified/Ident functors — min_sort never sees these (typer stores reflect shapes), doc clarified; WI-283/279 extend with a SymbolKind::Sort check if needed. PRE-EXISTING GAP: match-guard exprs are not typed/stamped, so min_sort(guard)=None (relevant to WI-282). min_sort returns Option<Symbol> = sort-head symbol, the WI-283/279 dispatch key.", at: "2026-05-22T16:15:05Z")
